Server Code (save as file_server.py)

import socket

server = socket.socket()
server.bind(('localhost', 6000))
server.listen(1)

print("Server ready... waiting for connection...")
conn, addr = server.accept()
print("Connected with:", addr)

file = open("received_file.txt", "wb")

data = conn.recv(1024)
while data:
    file.write(data)
    data = conn.recv(1024)

file.close()
conn.close()
server.close()
print("File received successfully.")


Client Code (save as file_client.py)

import socket

client = socket.socket()
client.connect(('localhost', 6000))

file = open("send_file.txt", "rb")

data = file.read(1024)
while data:
    client.send(data)
    data = file.read(1024)

file.close()
client.close()
print("File sent successfully.")





How to test

Create a file named send_file.txt in same folder.

Open Terminal 1:
python file_server.py

Open Terminal 2:
python file_client.py
